(56, 'Home', '3', 'home', '<p class=\"founder-degree\">(MBBS, MD, Fellow in Paediatrics, Autism Specialist)</p><ul class=\"founder-list\"><li>Visiting Faculty (Dept of Cell Biology, University of Melbourne, AUS)</li><li>Son-Rise Program (Autism Treatment Centre of America, MA, USA)</li><li>Post Graduate Diploma in Education Administration (Symbiosis)</li><li>Teachers Training in Special Education for Autism (ATI)</li><li>Ex Consultant MAMC &amp; AIIMS</li><li>Social activist</li><li>2-times TEDx speaker</li><li>Autism parent</li><li>Active Member of India Medical Association</li><li>On the advisory board panel of mainstream schools in Noida, Greater Noida, Ghaziabad &amp; Meerut</li></ul>', 'Meet the Founder', 'branch/assets/category/img1788264394.webp', '', '', '', '', '[]', 'Dr. Sonali Kataria Sirohi', 1, 4),
(58, 'About Us', '1', 'about-us', 'Sunrise Learning welcomes you and your family to a special school with an active-learning social environment. Its USP is the unique, secure and relaxed setting, where caring, sharing and cuddling are all significant parts of our daily activities. Sunrise Learning appreciates your confidence and trust, and hopes to partner with you and your family as we attempt to develop your ward ‘s Social, Emotional, Cognitive, Intellectual and Physical well-being along with you.', '', 'branch/assets/category/img1788346502.webp', '', '', '', NULL, NULL, 'Sunrise Learning Special School', 1, 1),
(59, 'About Us', '3', 'about-us', 'Just like any other person, even people with autism are on a continuum/ spectrum of being really interactive at one point of time in the day, and being very withdrawn or disconnected at another moment. And since Autism is a social-relational condition, many autistics tend to be more on the disconnected end of the spectrum, for more time. So, their social/ interactive state can be said to be towards the RED end of the spectrum, (when they are completely disconnected) OR towards GREEN end (when they are willing to interact). We utilize these RED & GREEN lights to respect the social state of mind of the student, INTERACT with them accordingly and train the parents to identify these lights. So during red lights, we can simply Join their world, to BOND, while during green lights, we can teach, learn, and play. That helps us in entering their bubble, inside their world. It is a way of accepting these people, with a non-judgmental attitude. And this approach helps to develop a stronger bond and connection between the teachers and the students, thus facilitating better learning outcomes.', '', 'branch/assets/category/img1788346938.webp', '', '', '', '', '[]', 'Some of our principles and approaches are inspired by the Son-Rise Program (Autism Treatment Center of America, MA,', 1, 2),
(60, 'About Us', '3', 'about-us', '<p><strong>Our Unique Value Proposition (USP): Lifespan Support for Neurodiverse Learners</strong></p>\r\n<p>At Sunrise Learning, our core strength lies in providing holistic, lifespan-based support for individuals with autism and other developmental challenges. Unlike conventional approaches that compartmentalize services across different stages and institutions, we offer a seamless continuum of care and education &mdash; all under one roof.</p>\r\n<p>What a neurotypical individual typically receives through four distinct systems across their life &mdash; preschool, school, college, and professional training &mdash; a neurodiverse learner at Sunrise Learning experiences in an integrated, personalized journey that adapts to their pace, needs, and potential.</p>\r\n<h4>Our Lifespan Model:</h4>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Early Intervention (Ages 2&ndash;6):</strong> Equivalent to preschool, focusing on foundational skills, communication, and sensory regulation.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Special Schooling (Ages 4&ndash;10 and Ages 8&ndash;16):</strong> Targeted learning for early learners, and for Pre-Vocational programs &ndash; developmental progress through structured programs and individual educational plans, with Emphasis on life skills, functional academics, and open schooling to build grade-level competencies for holistic development.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Vocational Skill Training (Ages 14&ndash;18):</strong> Equivalent to college-level learning, this phase offers exposure to real-life skills in hospitality, retail, IT, arts &amp; crafts, and other areas based on individual interests and strengths.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Employment &amp; Livelihood Readiness (18+):</strong> Tailored pathways for job readiness, micro-enterprise creation, and supported employment &mdash; equivalent to professional certification or actual employment in the neurotypical world.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>We do not follow a deficit-based model. Instead, our approach celebrates neurodiversity, fosters strengths, builds dignity, and promotes functional independence.</p>\r\n<p>Our belief is simple yet powerful: Development should not be fragmented. A break or gap in the support system can lead to regression. That&rsquo;s why our integrated model ensures continuity, predictability, and a sense of belonging throughout a learner&rsquo;s journey &mdash; from early childhood to adulthood.</p>', '', 'branch/assets/category/img1788349613.webp', '', '', '', 'Some more principles that we use and follow at Sunrise Learning:', '[{\"title\":\"Structured Teaching & Visual Supports\",\"desc\":\"Autistic & Special Needs people learn best through structured teaching methods, with visual supports. Therefore, schedules, labels (for clarity) and physical boundaries, clarity through pictures and visuals form an important part of our learning programs.\"},{\"title\":\"Routines & Transitions System\",\"desc\":\"People with autism love routines and have difficulties with transitions. So, we follow a well-researched schedule & planner system, with a versatile yet comprehensive curriculum, for bringing out the best in our students.\"},{\"title\":\"Social Stories & Context Preparation\",\"desc\":\"Autistics have difficulties in understanding context. Social stories are a great way to prepare them for different social contexts, and for small & big changes, and we use these customized stories to prepare them for every possible social situation.\"}]', 'OUR APPROACH', 1, 3),
(61, 'S L Foundation', '3', 's-l-foundation', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'Other Recognitions', '[{\"title\":\"Tulsabai Somani Educational Trust Award 2010\",\"desc\":\"Indian Association of Neurosciences 2010\"},{\"title\":\"Neurobiology of Autism Scholarship 2012\",\"desc\":\"Received scholarship for attending Advanced course on Neurobiology of Autism at Neuroscience School of Advanced Studies (NSAS), Italy.\"},{\"title\":\"Son-Rise Program Scholarship 2014\",\"desc\":\"Received scholarship for attending Start-up Son-Rise Program for Autism at Option Institute, Sheffield, MA, USA.\"},{\"title\":\"Rashtriya Gaurav Puraskar 2014\",\"desc\":\"Nominated for prestigious Rashtriya Gaurav Puraskar 2014 for exemplary social contribution.\"},{\"title\":\"Sofy Women\'s Awards 2015\",\"desc\":\"Nominated in Social Excellence category 2015 (conducted by Zee News).\"},{\"title\":\"19th Stree Shakti Award 2018\",\"desc\":\"Awarded by Gantavya Sansthan (presented by Shri Sunil Shastri, s\\/o Late Shri Lal Bahadur Shastri) for outstanding women empowerment.\"},{\"title\":\"PNI Achievers Award 2018\",\"desc\":\"Awarded for outstanding work in the field of empowerment of persons with special needs.\"},{\"title\":\"International School Award 2019 at Dubai\",\"desc\":\"Presented by Amity University at Dubai for phenomenal parental engagement and empowerment.\"}]', '', 1, 3),
(63, 'Parent Training', '3', 'parent-training', '<p>These powerful and short courses are meant for individuals who work with children or adults on the autism spectrum: Like parents of children with special needs or teachers working in inclusive main-stream schools, who have students with special needs in their regular classes.</p>\r\n<p>These simple, concise, comprehensive courses will provide you with an insight into the world of autism, and related conditions, not only from the professionals&rsquo; perspectives, but also from parents&rsquo; perspectives. The trainees will get a hands-on experience of working and interacting with children/ young adults with autism, in a structured environment of a special school, with trained and qualified faculty. The candidates who complete this certificate course can easily get connected with a child with autism, and help children/ adults with autism in various spheres of life, including helping as shadows.</p>', '', 'branch/assets/category/img1788427600.webp', '', '', '', 'Training Programs & Workshops', '[{\"title\":\"PARENTS EMPOWERMENT SATURDAYS (PES)\",\"desc\":\"Hands-on / Online training sessions for parents on Saturdays (Timings: 10 am to 1 pm).\"},{\"title\":\"PARENT EMPOWERMENT PROGRAMS (PEP)\",\"desc\":\"6-8 weeks regular hands-on training programs for parents on weekdays & some Saturdays. Timings: APPRX 2-3 hoursu2019 daily.\"},{\"title\":\"WORKSHOPS & SEMINARS\",\"desc\":\"Once a quarter regular in-house parentu2019s workshops on Saturdays (Timings: 10 am to 1 pm). 2 Annual 2-day workshops (Timings: 9 am to 5 pm) in April (Autism Awareness Month) and October (Sensory Processing Disorders Awareness Month). Daycare facility available ONLY on request basis for workshop.\"}]', '', 1, 2),
(64, 'Home', '3', 'home', '<p>Special School &amp; Vocational Training Center for children &amp; adults with special needs (autism, ADHD, Intellectual Disability, Downs Syndrome &amp; other neurodevelopmental conditions)</p><p><strong>Age groups:</strong> 2+ to 30+ years</p>', '\"Empowering Special Lives Towards Independence and Dignity Since 2014\"', 'branch/assets/category/img1788757780.webp', '', '', '', '', '[]', 'Sunrise Learning', 1, 1),
(65, 'Home', '3', 'home', '<p>SUNRISE LEARNING is a special school in Noida that offers school programs to children &amp; adults with autism &amp; other special needs. We work with children as young as 2 years (in Early Intervention) to adults 30+ years (for Employment Readiness Trainings). We offer several school programs that nurture holistic development of children, and provide an inclusive social environment for learners to progress towards independence &amp; dignity.</p>', 'SUNRISE LEARNING SPECIAL SCHOOL NOIDA', 'branch/assets/category/img1788758484.webp', '', '', '', '', '[]', 'ABOUT SUNRISE LEARNING', 1, 2),
(66, 'Home', '3', 'home', '<p><strong>Sunrise Learning Foundation welcomes you and your family to SUNRISE LEARNING &ndash; Outreach Support and Centre for Autism and Special Needs.</strong></p>\r\n<p>Our mandate is to look for the unique interests and strengths of a person on the spectrum and channelise that interest for his/her education and skill development.</p>\r\n<p>We work to create a stimulating, safe and nurturing environment for Social Emotional, Cognitive, Intellectual and Physical well-being of our students. Our focus is on using the right modules and tools to empower them with knowledge, education and skills to learn and become self-dependent.</p>\r\n<p>The team of educators, therapists, teachers specialists providing skill training &amp; education, as part of the special schooling, are Autism Specialists, Psychologists, Special Educators, Qualified Academic Teachers, AAC therapists, Computer ICT educators, Speech Language Pathologists, Occupational Therapists &amp; Consultant Paediatrician.</p>\r\n<p>With systems for assessments and technology-aided programs for early intervention, early learning center, pre-vocational skill training, speech and motor skill therapies, activities of daily living, computer education, NIOS education, vocational courses for employable skills, Sports Academy (registered with Special Olympics Bharat) and multidisciplinary activities like yoga, dance, music, app-based communication and art, we endeavour to create resources to empower parents to help their specially abled ward grow to his/her potential.</p>\r\n<p>Besides the direct trainings at the Noida center, most of our student and parents empowerment programs are offered on online platforms also, both as paid and free trainings.</p>\r\n<p><em>It\'s our endeavour to enable our students to live with independence and dignity in an inclusive world.</em></p>', 'Special School for persons with Autism & other special needs, for ages 2 years to 40+ years', 'branch/assets/category/img1788859510.webp', '', '', '', '', '[]', 'SUNRISE LEARNING', 1, 3),
(67, 'About Us', '3', 'about-us', '', '', '', '', '', '', 'For parents / professionals', '[{\"title\":\"Parents Empowerment Series (PES)\",\"desc\":\"\"},{\"title\":\"Parents Empowerment Programs (PEP)\",\"desc\":\"\"},{\"title\":\"Empowerment Training Courses\",\"desc\":\"\"},{\"title\":\"Certificate Courses\",\"desc\":\"\"},{\"title\":\"Internships & Volunteer Programs\",\"desc\":\"\"},{\"title\":\"Counselling Sessions\",\"desc\":\"\"}]', '', 1, 4);

